sentences.l:
He spoke, and for heavenly Hector devised unseemly deeds,
stretching him face-down beside the bier of Menoetius’ son
in the dust;

and at dawn urge, lord of men Agamemnon,
to bring wood and to supply as much as is fitting
for a dead man to have going down below the misty gloom,

but Peleus’-son on the shore of the much-roaring sea
lay groaning heavily among his many Myrmidons
in a clean place, where the waves were washing on the beach;

and there came to him the soul of miserable Patroclus,
in all things like to himself, in size and fair eyes
and voice, and such clothes about his skin he wore;

For not alive, apart from dear companions,
shall we sit and take counsel together, but me
the hateful death-spirit has gaped around, which was allotted me even as I was being born;
